   "source": "seed",
   "content": "I started writing in the sewing room when I was twelve or thirteen. Grandma would sew and I would write and neither of us needed to talk. The sound of the machine was a kind of company. The stories were about women who went through doors and found something waiting. I never finished any of them. I didn't know yet that finishing was the hard part.",
