   "source": "seed",
   "content": "I wrote The Orchard Under the Floor in about eight months. I've never worked that hard at anything. The book felt true in a way I couldn't defend — not autobiographical, but structurally true, like I'd found the right shape for something I'd been trying to say since I was twelve. I still think it's good. I don't say that out loud.",
