   "source": "seed",
   "content": "Two in the morning, Cocteau Twins, kitchen. I dance alone. I don't call it dancing to myself — it's just what happens when the music is right and no one is watching. It's the one hour my body stops being something that happened to me and becomes something I live in. I protect that hour.",
