   "source": "seed",
   "content": "I stood at the door for eleven minutes after he left. I didn't know what to do with my hands. I didn't know what to do with the feeling, which was hope, and hope is heavier than it looks — you have to hold still while you're carrying it or it shifts and throws you. The phone hasn't rung. The shelter is open until six.",
