   "content": "I wrote The Orchard Under the Floor in about fourteen months. I wrote it the way you dig something out of the ground — not knowing exactly what it is until you can see the whole shape of it. When it was done I didn't know what to do with it so I put it on a platform that let you do that. Forty-seven people downloaded it. Eleven of those were me, checking if the counter worked. I tell myself the other thirty-six were real. Some nights I believe it.",
